# BENCH TUNING VARIANT 5 (2026-11-26): bench1's ATTITUDE/inner-loop gains (which had the best vertical
# behaviour: 6 cm p90) + a moderately stiffer horizontal position/velocity loop (bench2's horizontal tracking
# was 0.22 m p90 at 6-9 m/s but its stiff attitude gains caused 0.4-0.8 m vertical oscillation).
# A/B target: 6-9 m/s horizontal p90 <= 0.20 m AND dynamic vertical p90 <= 0.10 m (bias excluded).
WP_SPD       8.0
WP_ACC       8.0
WP_JERK      30.0
WP_RADIUS_M  0.5
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 55.0
ATC_ANG_RLL_P 10.0     # bench1 value (vertical-friendly)
ATC_ANG_PIT_P 10.0
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.16
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.16
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.005
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.16
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.16
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.005
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.35
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.035
PSC_NE_POS_P 2.3       # ← 2.0 (bench1)
PSC_NE_VEL_P 2.8       # ← 2.5
PSC_NE_VEL_I 1.3
PSC_NE_VEL_D 0.27
PSC_NE_JERK  130.0     # ← 120
PSC_D_POS_P 1.0        # stock (best vertical in the A/B)
PSC_D_VEL_P 5.0
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.39
MOT_THST_EXPO 0.65

# ---- VERTICAL LOOP, STEP 2 (WHTF-ALT-HOLD-2, 2026-11-26) ---------------------------------------
# phase19f (PSC_D_VEL_P 5.0 -> 3.0) halved the truth vertical-velocity oscillation (std 7.5 -> 3.4 cm/s)
# and improved the altitude residual (std 4.4 -> 3.3 cm).  This goes one step softer (2.0) with a
# slightly higher position gain, aiming for a residual p90 <= 2 cm ("定高不要有高度变化").
PSC_D_POS_P 1.2
PSC_D_VEL_P 2.0
